WEBVTT

00:04.170 --> 00:05.020
Huh?

00:05.020 --> 00:06.270
Who's that guy?

00:14.960 --> 00:16.800
Hey, Boss! Wait up!

00:16.800 --> 00:18.870
You told me to do as I will, remember?!

00:19.110 --> 00:21.900
I had to bust up the roof to run after you.

00:22.620 --> 00:25.900
Your three minutes were already up.

00:30.810 --> 00:32.240
What's wrong?

00:32.240 --> 00:35.550
Oh, just a strange presence.

00:36.450 --> 00:37.810
Strange how?

02:10.850 --> 02:11.980
Sorry.

02:12.420 --> 02:14.650
I dragged you all into my problem.

02:14.650 --> 02:18.240
It's not only your problem anymore, Iwa-san.

02:18.240 --> 02:23.830
Although I do think you got too 
emotional about Inspector Hosorogi.

02:25.460 --> 02:30.000
Solitaire's involved, so this 
was always a case for Comps-3.

02:31.200 --> 02:32.700
That's right.

02:33.490 --> 02:38.550
Plus the media's onto the Habaki case, 
so it'll be big news.

02:38.550 --> 02:41.980
They might even go after you, sir.

02:42.320 --> 02:46.000
You might want to go incognito for a bit.

02:46.000 --> 02:48.140
Yatsu, Pops...

02:48.350 --> 02:51.930
Sorry we didn't manage to catch Habaki.

02:51.930 --> 02:53.290
No, it's fine.

02:54.160 --> 02:57.130
I'd like to get him before 
he flees the country,

02:57.610 --> 03:00.360
but we don't know the size or strength 
of the group we're up against.

03:01.060 --> 03:02.700
Don't take any chances.

03:02.910 --> 03:07.300
Yes. I hope we can settle this 
before that becomes a problem.

03:11.520 --> 03:14.770
I don't remember summoning you, 
Your Imperial Majesty.

03:14.770 --> 03:19.550
Have a heart. Appearing here wasn't easy,

03:19.800 --> 03:23.720
and you ignored our warnings 
a hundred years ago.

03:24.140 --> 03:26.500
Is it not your turn to yield?

03:29.690 --> 03:31.190
Have no fear.

03:31.400 --> 03:34.440
We came of our own accord 
and will soon vanish.

03:35.530 --> 03:39.840
Still, learning this world's 
language through you was a delight!

03:43.950 --> 03:45.870
He's so cute!

03:46.430 --> 03:48.810
What a fascinating world this is.

03:48.810 --> 03:50.830
The others long to see 
it for themselves, too.

03:51.770 --> 03:53.740
I'm sorry, but—

03:53.740 --> 03:54.810
Don't be.

03:55.210 --> 03:59.530
We'll wait patiently until 
your heart wants us here.

04:02.160 --> 04:04.900
One day, it will.

04:06.650 --> 04:07.550
Who is he?

04:07.970 --> 04:09.430
My friend.

04:09.430 --> 04:13.010
From the other world.

04:13.010 --> 04:13.970
I see.

04:14.380 --> 04:15.920
You have a good friend.

04:16.370 --> 04:18.420
Yes, I do.

04:19.220 --> 04:22.280
<i>Although I don't know if 
he'll be good for this world.</i>

04:25.500 --> 04:30.490
You're still you, 
and we are still us, dear friend.

04:33.140 --> 04:36.130
In life or in death.

04:37.810 --> 04:41.840
Now, we told you not to think of revenge,

04:41.840 --> 04:45.970
but we did not mean you should
 abandon hatred and become a saint.

04:50.410 --> 04:52.490
This is partly a whim of ours.

04:56.180 --> 05:00.230
P-Please... stop!

05:00.710 --> 05:01.690
Izliz.

05:09.770 --> 05:14.500
The old hag and I didn't want 
to show you, Corpse God.

05:14.500 --> 05:20.310
I'm sorry! F-Forgive me!

05:22.820 --> 05:27.510
Taking on our subjects' dirty 
work is what we're here for!

05:27.910 --> 05:28.970
So...

05:29.370 --> 05:32.930
You needn't sully yourself, dear friend.

05:43.070 --> 05:48.030
Egotistical thinking like that got 
Your Imperial Majesty assassinated.

05:48.910 --> 05:50.240
Maybe so!

05:53.630 --> 05:56.080
It's gone?

05:56.770 --> 06:01.040
I planned to observe a little longer, 
but I'll make my move tomorrow.

06:01.770 --> 06:04.860
This city seems full of 
troublesome residents.

06:05.620 --> 06:08.480
Between the Bug and my compatriot,

06:08.480 --> 06:10.840
who should I see to first?

06:12.160 --> 06:16.090
My wish hasn't changed, 
Your Imperial Majesty.

06:17.050 --> 06:19.540
I want a world where we 
can all live in peace.

06:20.370 --> 06:23.880
A world where you won't 
need to dirty your hands.

06:24.260 --> 06:25.550
That's why

06:26.130 --> 06:29.660
I need to get more involved.

06:30.390 --> 06:35.180
To reach where the shadows of 
that world mingle with this one.

06:38.550 --> 06:39.960
Habaki-san,

06:39.960 --> 06:45.000
I hope the higher-ups take care 
of you before you squeal on me.

06:45.650 --> 06:47.970
<i>Should I lie low?</i>

06:48.490 --> 06:52.140
<i>I'd better dispose of this 
phone in the next few hou—</i>

06:52.340 --> 06:53.140
Hot!

06:54.310 --> 06:56.850
Dearie me. You dropped this.

06:56.850 --> 06:59.040
Thanks. Sorry to bother y—

06:59.040 --> 06:59.640
Huh?

07:00.170 --> 07:02.100
Hey! What the—?!

07:02.100 --> 07:03.060
Excuse me, but—

07:03.690 --> 07:05.390
Hands. Feet.

07:05.390 --> 07:07.890
Sabaramond's...

07:07.890 --> 07:08.570
Eyes.

07:08.570 --> 07:09.580
Ears.

07:09.580 --> 07:11.860
Catch him-im-im.

07:11.860 --> 07:15.410
Maybe running wasn't such 
a great idea after all.

07:16.640 --> 07:18.910
Oh, hi. Polka-kun?

07:19.130 --> 07:22.890
We're back at the building now. Are you okay?

07:22.890 --> 07:23.710
<i>Yes.</i>

07:23.710 --> 07:26.400
<i>I'm with Clarissa-san now.</i>

07:26.400 --> 07:28.030
Will duct tape work?

07:28.030 --> 07:29.340
For now.

07:30.530 --> 07:32.050
They're really well-made.

07:33.170 --> 07:34.750
You aren't surprised?

07:35.100 --> 07:36.930
Why would I be?

07:37.250 --> 07:40.090
This is Shinoyama tech, right?

07:40.090 --> 07:44.080
I've asked the same company
 to make me robot sharks before.

07:44.080 --> 07:45.900
O-Oh, I see.

07:46.220 --> 07:51.930
Besides, I knew you were 
hiding a secret or two.

07:52.830 --> 07:55.590
I'd be surprised if one were 
turning into a tiny shark.

07:55.590 --> 07:58.550
Then I'd ask you to marry me.

07:58.550 --> 08:00.250
M-Marry y—?!

08:00.510 --> 08:03.730
I can figure some things out 
even if you don't tell me.

08:04.280 --> 08:07.180
You've been working to protect us, right?

08:08.680 --> 08:09.800
Thank you.

08:12.060 --> 08:13.050
<i>No.</i>

08:13.410 --> 08:14.580
<i>You're wrong.</i>

08:14.580 --> 08:16.010
<i>I did it</i>

08:16.380 --> 08:18.150
<i>all for myself.</i>

08:18.150 --> 08:20.260
Kurupon, they want to talk to you.

08:21.470 --> 08:23.280
Hello. Takumi-kun?

08:23.280 --> 08:27.330
I hear you hurt your leg. 
Come to the bar later.

08:27.990 --> 08:31.160
I'll ask Kazami to treat 
you and issue medicine.

08:31.160 --> 08:33.320
Oh, it's no big deal.

08:33.320 --> 08:34.400
Once the bleeding stops, I'll be—

08:34.400 --> 08:36.470
<i>Stop arguing and get it fixed up.</i>

08:38.090 --> 08:40.150
Injuries should scare you.

08:40.150 --> 08:42.770
If you don't heal them properly,

08:42.770 --> 08:45.040
they'll come back to haunt you.

08:45.690 --> 08:48.750
<i>I knew it, Clarissa. Your eyesight is...</i>

08:49.360 --> 08:52.290
<i>Polka, I want you to ask 
Lisa something for me.</i>

08:54.030 --> 08:59.730
Umm... How did you know that man,
 Habaki, was, well...

09:00.280 --> 09:01.430
Are you curious?

09:03.310 --> 09:07.400
Well, all I've done is put down roots.

09:08.110 --> 09:12.360
I couldn't have reached him without 
tips from a police insider.

09:12.360 --> 09:14.610
<i>What? Who could it be?</i>

09:15.450 --> 09:17.770
You can locate Habaki, I presume?

09:15.630 --> 09:18.570
<b>One 
Hour Ago</b>

09:17.770 --> 09:18.570
<i>Yes.</i>

09:18.780 --> 09:22.210
<i>I stuck a GPS chip on his sleeve.</i>

09:22.210 --> 09:25.040
And you're fine with this, Tozawa-san?

09:25.040 --> 09:27.750
Yes. I used my own judgment.

09:28.250 --> 09:32.210
I know my grandfather saved your wife,

09:32.580 --> 09:35.490
but is that debt worth 
betraying Tsubaki Iwanome?

09:35.800 --> 09:37.430
Debts don't enter into it.

09:38.120 --> 09:42.390
I think this case is bigger 
than even the troublemakers.

09:42.740 --> 09:46.410
I want Inspector Iwanome to 
stay an honest police officer.

09:47.330 --> 09:51.150
I'd hate to see him go astray like I did.

09:51.150 --> 09:53.290
<i>You're a regular mother hen.</i>

09:53.790 --> 09:57.240
He's strong, but he's still fragile.

09:57.710 --> 10:03.910
I want him—and all of Comps-3—to walk 
the straight and narrow until they mature.

10:04.450 --> 10:06.840
That's all there is to it.

10:08.120 --> 10:12.470
Okay! Start with another look at Senior 
Commissioner Habaki's call history.

10:12.470 --> 10:14.840
Check security cameras in 
HQ and on the streets, too.

10:15.100 --> 10:18.700
Follow up on any contact with Habaki 
or the officer who committed suicide.

10:18.700 --> 10:19.680
Yes, sir!

10:20.030 --> 10:22.640
<b>Don't be a prisoner of the past.
 At least choose your indulgences yourself.
 
Corruption is eating away from the top.
 Don't trust anyone. 

There's another garage on
 the west side of that place. 
The signpost is inside. 

The key is behind the mirror of I-383.</b>

10:20.030 --> 10:22.640
<b>m 0 0 l 400 0 400 400 0 400</b>

10:20.730 --> 10:22.640
Arase, you and me will work on this.

10:22.850 --> 10:25.090
You seem awfully enthusiastic.

10:25.090 --> 10:28.270
Sorry, but I'm probably still emotional.

10:28.620 --> 10:31.990
I've figured out that I can't 
track down Hosorogi-san,

10:32.420 --> 10:35.030
so I'll have to make Hosorogi-san come to me.

10:35.030 --> 10:37.990
That's easy enough to say, but how, exactly?

10:37.990 --> 10:39.460
Strong-arm tactics.

10:39.830 --> 10:42.950
I'll smoke out the organization 
Habaki belonged to.

10:43.320 --> 10:46.330
"Sabaramond" is probably the keyword.

10:46.740 --> 10:50.150
Everyone in their pocket is going down.

10:50.150 --> 10:54.380
I'm just going to make a place 
Hosorogi-san can come back to.

10:54.960 --> 10:59.630
If, er, I managed to find 
Hosorogi-san's soul,

10:59.630 --> 11:01.840
would you like me to deliver a message?

11:01.840 --> 11:02.590
Hmm?

11:02.980 --> 11:03.920
<i>Polka?!</i>

11:04.250 --> 11:05.900
<i>I'm sorry I didn't ask you first.</i>

11:06.430 --> 11:07.500
Let me think.

11:08.660 --> 11:11.530
I trampled on Miyabi-san's wishes.

11:12.590 --> 11:16.530
Miyabi-san never wanted me 
to become what I am now.

11:17.090 --> 11:22.220
An intermediary, inheriting the secret 
family trade like my grandfather wanted.

11:23.090 --> 11:25.740
But this is who I am now.

11:26.330 --> 11:29.460
There's no getting around that,
 and I don't regret it.

11:29.990 --> 11:34.500
So, if I could send a message, 
it would be just one thing.

11:34.500 --> 11:39.460
When the inspector comes back, 
I know just what to say first.

11:39.930 --> 11:41.050
Hosorogi-san,

11:41.540 --> 11:44.890
goodbye, my love.

11:44.890 --> 11:47.260
it's good to have you back!

11:56.580 --> 11:57.750
Um...

11:58.740 --> 12:00.500
Where the hell am I?

11:58.920 --> 12:04.320
<b>Fire
Safety</b>

12:00.500 --> 12:03.530
So, you're awake.

12:09.910 --> 12:11.050
Who's he?

12:13.210 --> 12:15.250
Misaki-chan. Takumi-kun.

12:17.500 --> 12:18.500
Welcome back!

12:18.800 --> 12:21.910
Misaki-chan, you seem fine.

12:21.910 --> 12:24.470
Yup! Never been better!

12:24.950 --> 12:26.050
Takumi-kun.

12:26.730 --> 12:29.370
I could cast a spell to repair 
your body, if you'd like.

12:29.370 --> 12:31.140
Huh? You can do that?

12:31.410 --> 12:34.160
If I temporarily render part of you a corpse...

12:34.160 --> 12:36.020
Nah, I'm good with normal medicine.

12:36.020 --> 12:39.020
I'll take you up on that if I 
ever get a fatal wound, though.

12:39.810 --> 12:40.600
Okay.

12:41.630 --> 12:43.400
<i>I can't leave things as they are.</i>

12:44.030 --> 12:46.830
<i>If I want a world where I can 
live in peace with everyone,</i>

12:47.330 --> 12:50.000
<i>I ought to take the initiative and step up.</i>

12:50.540 --> 12:54.030
<i>To face this world as the Corpse God.</i>

12:55.510 --> 12:56.640
Hmm...

12:56.640 --> 12:58.380
May I have a moment?

12:58.690 --> 13:01.680
Who is this man sitting here?

13:01.680 --> 13:05.740
An innocent bystander who learned 
the Fire-Breathing Bug's identity?

13:05.740 --> 13:07.340
I think not.

13:07.620 --> 13:10.410
He probably works with Habaki,

13:11.400 --> 13:15.600
which would mean he's 
involved with this symbol.

13:16.040 --> 13:19.800
You've been incinerating every 
member of the organization,

13:19.800 --> 13:24.420
but perhaps you've sensed 
the limits of that strategy.

13:24.420 --> 13:29.410
Now that the organization is exposed, 
the situation will change considerably.

13:30.060 --> 13:33.870
And so, you tried a new approach!

13:34.160 --> 13:38.360
You'll reach the organization's 
root to crush it!

13:38.360 --> 13:45.590
So you turned to me, the man who 
flushed out this fellow and Habaki.

13:46.570 --> 13:48.800
Exactly.

13:49.030 --> 13:50.640
You catch on quick.

13:50.640 --> 13:51.890
I knew I could count on you.

13:51.890 --> 13:57.020
Talk can be vital to the magician's art.
 That was simplicity itself.

13:57.020 --> 14:00.280
To reach this level, I...

13:57.410 --> 14:01.140
<i>I pegged him as just a 
criminal with a screw loose,</i>

14:00.280 --> 14:04.560
The magician is operating! The magician 
is operating! The magician is operating!

14:01.450 --> 14:05.740
<i>but did he plan this down 
to every last detail?</i>

14:04.560 --> 14:05.740
And there you have it!

14:05.740 --> 14:08.230
<i>I can't believe I guessed right!</i>

14:08.230 --> 14:12.780
<i>I even had a pratfall ready 
for when they said no!</i>

14:11.050 --> 14:11.430
<b><b>FWOOMP!</b></b>

14:13.110 --> 14:16.800
Uh... I have no idea what 
you're talking about.

14:16.800 --> 14:18.500
Can I please go home now?

14:19.000 --> 14:19.960
Hmm...

14:21.110 --> 14:25.530
Rubbing elbows with troublemakers has 
given me a nose for these things.

14:26.250 --> 14:30.140
You smell like you've killed multiple people.

14:30.440 --> 14:34.100
So whatever I do to you, 
I'll get away with it—or die!

14:34.340 --> 14:37.120
Do you have a scientific basis for that?

14:37.120 --> 14:42.080
If I turned out to be a normal guy, 
wouldn't that wound your pride?

14:43.490 --> 14:44.890
Worry not.

14:44.890 --> 14:47.150
My pride is still

14:47.150 --> 14:48.680
in prison.

14:47.150 --> 14:50.360
<b>Pride</b>

14:48.680 --> 14:50.360
I... I see?

14:50.700 --> 14:54.830
Besides, I've been a nuisance 
to ordinary people for ages!

14:55.100 --> 15:01.450
A bunch of stocks took a nosedive when 
I kidnapped Prime Minister Kubikigawara.

15:03.080 --> 15:06.000
Solitaire reportedly infiltrated 
police headquarters.

15:06.250 --> 15:08.530
Damn that thrill-seeker.

15:09.130 --> 15:11.970
I see there was activity 
at Polka's building, too.

15:11.970 --> 15:12.970
Yes, sir.

15:12.970 --> 15:19.370
The data broker is wounded, and Miss 
Sayo's bodyguard lost a prosthetic arm.

15:19.750 --> 15:23.940
I suspect they engaged a hostile force.

15:24.170 --> 15:25.970
You sound detached.

15:25.970 --> 15:28.400
Isn't that bodyguard a Lei, like you?

15:28.400 --> 15:33.110
No, we've cut ties.
 He doesn't need my concern.

15:33.350 --> 15:36.330
Still, he is fairly capable.

15:36.330 --> 15:40.790
Meaning they weren't 
fighting common hoodlums.

15:40.790 --> 15:44.040
<b>Mikan</b>

15:44.410 --> 15:48.180
I suspect the enemy is already 
reaching for this place.

15:48.180 --> 15:49.260
Oh?

15:49.500 --> 15:51.550
Multiple sentries since last night.

15:51.550 --> 15:56.180
Someone knocked them out 
and took all their phones.

15:56.420 --> 15:59.890
So, they want information.

16:00.310 --> 16:05.160
And, strangely, my entire savings 
have vanished from my bank account.

16:05.770 --> 16:08.050
They're even targeting individuals?

16:08.050 --> 16:09.640
Look into it, Bao.

16:09.640 --> 16:10.770
On it.

16:10.770 --> 16:14.260
<b><i>00:00 current time

Tiered-Rate Savings 
(Standard)
Sales Dept. 0123456 

Account Balance:
 237,380,000 yen

 Deposit - Yanmei Lei
237,380,000 yen
 Balance: 237,380,000 yen</i></b>

16:10.770 --> 16:14.260
m 0 0 l 180 0 180 190 0 190

16:11.930 --> 16:14.260
I really did get a huge deposit.

16:14.260 --> 16:16.740
<b>From: Big Sis
Dear Little Brother, 

 Please don't say such sad things. 
Whatever Dad or the big lug say, 
I, at least, love, love, love, love, love you, 
and you're worth the world to me. To prove it,
 I'll empty out Taipei's bank account
 for talking down to you and deposit his money 
in your account, so don't give up
 your your big sis, okay? 

 Your knight in shining armor, Imbi</b>

16:14.260 --> 16:16.740
m 0 0 l 450 0 450 550 0 500

16:14.810 --> 16:16.740
My sister doesn't hold back.

16:17.370 --> 16:21.200
But anyway, I need to report 
the arm to His Lordship.

16:27.150 --> 16:28.880
<i>Hi. It's me.</i>

16:28.880 --> 16:30.340
<i>I heard the news.</i>

16:30.340 --> 16:33.090
<i>One of your arms got scrapped, right?</i>

16:33.090 --> 16:33.870
Huh?!

16:33.870 --> 16:36.860
Oh, y-yes. In a fight with the Agakuras.

16:36.860 --> 16:39.060
<i>Yeah, I heard that, too.</i>

16:39.060 --> 16:40.220
Huh?

16:40.680 --> 16:43.220
<i>First of all, I'm glad you're alive.</i>

16:43.540 --> 16:46.690
<i>And you kept the people in 
that building safe, too.</i>

16:46.900 --> 16:48.640
<i>Good work.</i>

16:48.640 --> 16:50.940
<i>Thanks, Xiaoyu.</i>

16:52.900 --> 16:55.920
Y-You don't need to thank me, Your Lordship!

16:55.920 --> 16:59.050
<i>So, what about the other arm and your legs?</i>

16:59.050 --> 17:00.870
They're fine.

17:01.400 --> 17:03.560
But this one was completely destroyed,

17:03.560 --> 17:06.830
so I guess I'll be going 
one-armed for a while.

17:07.210 --> 17:10.460
I'm so sorry. I broke a 
gift from Your Lordship.

17:10.460 --> 17:11.720
<i>Don't sweat it.</i>

17:11.720 --> 17:17.860
<i>And the guy behind you says 
he'll help with the arm.</i>

17:17.860 --> 17:18.800
Behind me?

17:20.480 --> 17:22.170
<i>When did he get here?!</i>

17:22.590 --> 17:27.550
Xiaoyu-kun, I heard that you 
tried to save Takumi-kun.

17:27.990 --> 17:32.190
I only stepped in because 
Miss Sayo might have been at risk.

17:32.190 --> 17:35.700
Would you let me get a new arm for you?

17:36.890 --> 17:39.650
Guarding the Shinoyamas is my job.

17:40.130 --> 17:43.240
That means I can't trust you.

17:45.340 --> 17:49.210
You were under the floor in 
Rozan-san's room, weren't you?

17:49.690 --> 17:52.920
I could tell right away because your 
soul has such a distinctive hue,

17:53.530 --> 17:57.760
so I also realized that you know I'm a fake.

17:57.760 --> 18:01.100
My soul's hue? What are you talking about?

18:01.100 --> 18:03.850
I'll explain that and everything else.

18:04.610 --> 18:05.980
So, to start off,

18:05.980 --> 18:08.600
I'd like you to challenge 
you to a serious fight.

18:08.600 --> 18:09.600
Huh?

18:16.490 --> 18:21.150
<i>Perfect. I'll expose him 
in front of His Lordship.</i>

18:22.650 --> 18:26.530
Don't expect me to just hang my 
head with His Lordship watching.

18:26.530 --> 18:27.710
Of course not.

18:28.090 --> 18:32.490
You rescued Takumi-kun. 
You don't need to bow.

18:32.840 --> 18:35.190
Enough talk. Just get ready.

18:35.190 --> 18:37.230
Oh, you won't be fighting me.

18:38.190 --> 18:42.150
Although you will face my power, 
so maybe it's the same thing.

18:44.490 --> 18:46.850
Your opponents are these dual-fanged tigers.

18:47.990 --> 18:49.940
I can't keep this up for too long,

18:50.240 --> 18:52.900
but please try to show me 
what you're capable of.

18:54.860 --> 18:56.440
<i>What the hell is that monster?!</i>

18:56.770 --> 18:58.670
<i>An illusion?! Hypnosis?!</i>

18:59.970 --> 19:04.740
<i>Well, I'll be. Your skills are even 
more impressive than I thought.</i>

19:05.060 --> 19:09.710
<i>I got a real fright when you 
called me up last night.</i>

19:10.440 --> 19:13.940
<i>After all, the Agakuras 
took his arms and legs.</i>

19:13.940 --> 19:18.050
<i>I worried he'd lose control 
and put himself in harm's way.</i>

19:18.420 --> 19:22.850
It's easy to say, "Don't overdo it.
 Run away if you want."

19:23.210 --> 19:24.760
But he's the type

19:24.760 --> 19:28.270
who'll push himself even harder if I do.

19:28.270 --> 19:29.230
I understand.

19:29.610 --> 19:34.690
I've seen many people put their 
feelings before their lives.

19:35.040 --> 19:39.050
<i>Still, if you let Xiaoyu 
in on your secret, too,</i>

19:39.050 --> 19:42.660
<i>you may end up further from 
a peaceful life than ever.</i>

19:45.090 --> 19:46.350
You have a point.

19:46.950 --> 19:51.510
But I'll just end up losing 
things if I hold back,

19:52.480 --> 19:57.630
so for the sake of the future, 
I've decided to push peace back for a while.

19:58.920 --> 19:59.510
That's enough.

20:02.090 --> 20:03.690
I get the gist now.

20:03.690 --> 20:05.980
Thanks, Gufa, Rafa.

20:08.000 --> 20:09.570
Huh?!

20:09.570 --> 20:10.480
Hey!

20:10.480 --> 20:12.350
Wha— Hey!

20:11.210 --> 20:14.440
I'm sorry. I guess they've 
taken a liking to you.

20:16.050 --> 20:20.760
For starters, you... er,
 you might want to take a shower.

20:24.610 --> 20:27.010
If my right arm and legs 
were in better shape—

20:28.000 --> 20:31.330
No. I went all-out in that fight.

20:31.660 --> 20:32.890
But him?

20:33.330 --> 20:38.920
That incomprehensible power was 
probably nowhere near his best.

20:40.920 --> 20:42.980
Oh, welcome back.

20:42.980 --> 20:44.870
Here's how they connect.

20:45.200 --> 20:48.720
So, can you do something about my arm?

20:49.530 --> 20:50.610
Thank you.

20:54.180 --> 20:55.270
What's your name?

20:55.270 --> 20:56.290
Huh?

20:56.290 --> 20:58.360
You must have a real name.

20:59.140 --> 21:01.670
Your strength is the real deal.

21:00.090 --> 21:00.460
<b>Mecha!</b>

21:00.710 --> 21:01.090
<b>Mecha!</b>

21:01.340 --> 21:01.710
<b>Cyborg!</b>

21:01.960 --> 21:02.340
<b>Cyborg!</b>

21:02.030 --> 21:05.340
Calling you "fake" like I have 
been wouldn't sit right with me.

21:02.340 --> 21:05.340
<b>Jumping 
(The Shark)
 For Joy</b>

21:02.340 --> 21:05.340
<b>m 0 0 l 140 0 140 80 0 80</b>

21:06.250 --> 21:08.070
If you don't mind a nickname,

21:08.560 --> 21:10.590
I'm the Corpse God.

21:11.850 --> 21:14.360
That's one hell of a nickname.

21:14.360 --> 21:17.040
Well, I don't disagree.

21:17.250 --> 21:22.300
Anyway, I can't believe that whole 
match was to tune my new arm.

21:22.910 --> 21:25.910
I put my life and my pride 
on the line, you know?

21:26.990 --> 21:29.760
So, what have you got for me?

21:30.060 --> 21:31.460
Oh, right.

21:31.460 --> 21:32.520
It's done.

21:34.700 --> 21:36.290
Wh-What the...?

21:36.730 --> 21:38.300
Where did this arm come from?!

21:40.230 --> 21:42.230
I want answers, Corpse God!

21:42.990 --> 21:44.380
Urdwigia.

21:44.890 --> 21:49.240
It's the right arm of the colossal dragon 
whose lightning once lit the world.

21:49.700 --> 21:50.590
A dragon?

21:52.330 --> 21:53.550
Xiaoyu-kun.

21:54.680 --> 21:57.250
I want to strike a deal 
in exchange for this arm.

21:57.630 --> 22:01.000
As the fourth-ranked imperial court sorcerer,

22:01.610 --> 22:03.540
I'm asking you for an alliance.
